.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-WALLPAPER 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-wallpapers 0.3.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-wallpaper \- pick the desktop wallpaper for the current theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-wallpaper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-wallpaper
shows the available wallpapers with thumbnail previews in a
.BR yad (1)
window, or as a plain
.BR wofi (1)
list if yad is not installed.
The one you pick is applied right away.
.PP
Each theme remembers its own wallpaper: the choice is saved for the theme
that is active now, and is used again whenever you switch back to that
theme with
.BR paperweight\-theme (1).
.PP
It is the
.B Wallpaper
entry in
.BR paperweight\-settings (1),
and can also be found by typing \(lqwallpaper\(rq into the app launcher.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/paperweight\-os/wallpapers/
Wallpapers shipped with PaperweightOS.
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/
Images here (PNG, JPEG or WebP) are offered too, in the yad picker.
.TP
.I ~/.config/paperweight\-os/wallpapers/<theme>
The saved choice for each theme: a single line with the image path.
Delete it to go back to that theme's default wallpaper.
.TP
.I ~/.config/paperweight\-os/active\-theme
Name of the current theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight\-theme (1),
.BR paperweight\-settings (1),
.BR swaybg (1)
